dialog 1.3-20260107 through 1.3-20260721: auto-sized menu/checklist/radiolist
lists are one row short.

The 2026/01/07 layout change reduces the height reserved for an auto-sized
box ("0 0 0", or "0 0 1") by one row via adjust_size, but the list height
calculated afterwards from the actual box height does not add that row back.
The result is a list one row shorter than the number of items, with an
unused blank row under it, so the last item has to be scrolled to even
though the box was sized to fit it.

Add adjust_size back when the list height is derived from the box height,
as is already done for specific_size.

Applies to menubox.c (menu, inputmenu is unaffected since its adjust_size
is always 0) and checklist.c (checklist, radiolist).

--- a/menubox.c	2026-11-24 06:35:28.507005633 +0000
+++ b/menubox.c	2026-11-24 06:35:28.603245014 +0000
@@ -457,6 +457,8 @@
     all.menu_height = height - MIN_HIGH - cur_y - 2;
     if (specific_size)
 	all.menu_height++;
+    /* give back the row that was taken from the auto-sized height */
+    all.menu_height += adjust_size;
     if (all.menu_height <= 0)
 	all.menu_height = 1;
 
--- a/checklist.c	2026-11-24 06:35:28.505774933 +0000
+++ b/checklist.c	2026-11-24 06:35:28.603471718 +0000
@@ -318,6 +318,8 @@
     all.use_height = height - MIN_HIGH - cur_y - 2;
     if (specific_size)
 	all.use_height++;
+    /* give back the row that was taken from the auto-sized height */
+    all.use_height += adjust_size;
     if (all.use_height <= 0)
 	all.use_height = 1;

